Feature: local players 2-4 share player 1's profile (two-player co-op on one PC)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0011-local-players-share-profile.patch
Status:     local patch (a feature for our port; the default behaviour is unchanged)

WHY
  A 360 game wants a gamer profile signed in on every player's controller.
  The SDK has one profile and answers only for user 0: XamUserGetSigninState,
  GetXUID, GetSigninInfo, GetName, GetGamerTag, Read/WriteProfileSettings,
  CheckPrivilege, the content restriction calls, GetMembershipTier and
  AreUsersFriends all say "no such user" for users 1-3. A PC has one player
  profile, so local co-op partners can't sign in at all.

WHAT
  rex/system/xam/user_profile.h gets a small API:
    SetLocalPlayerPresentCallback(fn)  the app says which users 1-3 are
                                       present (e.g. a controller plays as them)
    IsLocalUserSignedIn(user)          user 0: the profile's state; users 1-3:
                                       user 0 signed in AND the callback says yes
    SignedInUserMask()                 bit N = user N signed in
    NotifyLocalPlayersChanged()        broadcasts XN_SYS_SIGNINCHANGED (0xA) with
                                       the mask, so the game rebuilds its list
  The functions listed above answer for a present user 1-3 exactly as for
  user 0: same profile, same XUID and name, same settings. Saves were already
  stored by the profile's XUID whatever the user index (xam_content.cpp), so
  every player's saves land in the one profile. No callback = user 0 only, as
  before.

HOW WE FOUND / CHECKED IT (2026-10-02)
  Crash: Mind over Mutant with a controller assigned to player 2 (our input
  device assignment): pressing Start on that controller at "Press START" gave
  "You do not have an active gamer profile. You will be unable to save...".
  The game builds a signed-in mask by calling XamUserGetSigninState for users
  0-3 (sub_8227B1D8 on XN_SYS_SIGNINCHANGED, sub_8227CEA8) and refuses a
  player whose bit is clear: exactly what a real 360 does with no profile on
  controller 2. With this patch and our callback (a device plays as that player),
  see docs/findings/23 for the result.
